WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.767 --> 00:00:02.434
[ Heart beating ]

00:00:02.434 --> 00:00:04.434
[ Eerie music plays ]

00:00:04.434 --> 00:00:10.868
♪♪

00:00:10.868 --> 00:00:12.868
-Hello, Jimmy.

00:00:12.868 --> 00:00:14.400
-Come play with us.

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:16.834
-Come play with us, Jimmy.

00:00:16.834 --> 00:00:18.901
-Forever and ever.

00:00:18.901 --> 00:00:21.167
-And ever, and ever.

00:00:21.167 --> 00:00:23.267
♪♪

00:00:23.267 --> 00:00:25.200
-Okay.
What should we do?

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:26.334
-Want to help us
pick paint colors?

00:00:26.334 --> 00:00:27.334
-Sure.

00:00:27.334 --> 00:00:29.467
-And murder Higgins?

00:00:29.467 --> 00:00:30.601
-You bet.

00:00:30.601 --> 00:00:33.267
-This one's called "redrum."

00:00:33.267 --> 00:00:35.901
-Ooh, nice.

00:00:35.901 --> 00:00:36.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:36.901 --> 00:00:38.767
♪♪

00:00:38.767 --> 00:00:41.100
-From Studio 6B
in Rockefeller Center

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:42.501
in the heart of New York City,

00:00:42.501 --> 00:00:46.701
it's "The Tonight Show
starring Jimmy Fallon."

00:00:46.701 --> 00:00:48.234
-♪ Hey, hey hey, hey ♪

00:00:48.234 --> 00:00:50.100
-Tonight,
join Jimmy and his guests...

00:00:55.067 --> 00:00:57.000
Musical guest...

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.634
And featuring the legendary
Roots crew.

00:00:59.634 --> 00:01:01.968
-1775.

00:01:01.968 --> 00:01:08.901
-And now, here he is,
Jimmy Fallon!

00:01:08.901 --> 00:01:11.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:14.767
♪♪

00:01:14.767 --> 00:01:16.901
-Hey, come on.
Guys...

00:01:16.901 --> 00:01:18.634
[ Cheers and applause
continues ]

00:01:18.634 --> 00:01:21.200
Oh, that's very nice.
I appreciate that.

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:22.968
Thank you very much.
Hey!

00:01:22.968 --> 00:01:25.067
Welcome!
Nice to see you!

00:01:25.067 --> 00:01:26.400
Nice to see you.

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:28.133
Welcome, welcome, welcome,
welcome, welcome, welcome!

00:01:28.133 --> 00:01:31.067
-♪ Ooh, ooh, ooh, ooh ♪

00:01:31.067 --> 00:01:34.467
-Oh, my goodness.
Enjoy yourself.

00:01:34.467 --> 00:01:35.701
Welcome, everybody.

00:01:35.701 --> 00:01:38.501
Welcome, welcome, welcome
to "The Tonight Show."

00:01:38.501 --> 00:01:40.334
You're here.
You have made it.

00:01:40.334 --> 00:01:42.601
Thank you for watching at home.

00:01:42.601 --> 00:01:44.167
Well, guys, everyone
is talking about this --

00:01:44.167 --> 00:01:47.367
early this morning, all flights
across the U.S. were grounded

00:01:47.367 --> 00:01:50.801
due to a failure with the FAA's
computer system.

00:01:50.801 --> 00:01:52.667
Yeah.
Zero flights took off,

00:01:52.667 --> 00:01:55.200
but somehow everyone's luggage
still ended up in Pittsburgh.

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:57.667
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.667 --> 00:01:59.734
That's right.
No flights took off.

00:01:59.734 --> 00:02:01.734
It's never a good sign
when you see a jumbo jet

00:02:01.734 --> 00:02:03.567
taking the I-95 to Tampa.

00:02:03.567 --> 00:02:05.634
You know what I'm saying?
[ Laughter ]

00:02:05.634 --> 00:02:07.300
It's never fun
being stuck in an airport.

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:08.934
Families headed to Disney
told their kids

00:02:08.934 --> 00:02:11.601
the luggage carousel was the
"It's a Small World" ride.

00:02:11.601 --> 00:02:14.467
They're like, "Just calm down
and sit next to the Tumi bag.

00:02:14.467 --> 00:02:17.200
I'll take your picture."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:19.167
Yeah, no one could fix
the computer glitch.

00:02:19.167 --> 00:02:20.801
One guy at the FAA said,
"I don't know.

00:02:20.801 --> 00:02:22.534
Maybe unplug it,
plug it back in?

00:02:22.534 --> 00:02:24.234
I don't know."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.234 --> 00:02:25.534
Meanwhile, the outage happened

00:02:25.534 --> 00:02:28.934
while some planes
were in the air.

00:02:28.934 --> 00:02:30.868
If there's one thing you don't
want to hear from your pilot,

00:02:30.868 --> 00:02:33.033
it's "Attention, passengers --
do yourselves a favor

00:02:33.033 --> 00:02:34.601
and stay off Twitter
for a little bit."

00:02:34.601 --> 00:02:38.167
[ Laughter ]

00:02:38.167 --> 00:02:41.334
Thankfully, no one flying on
JetBlue could see the news,

00:02:41.334 --> 00:02:43.667
'cause all the TVs were broken.
But I mean, that's --

00:02:43.667 --> 00:02:45.200
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:47.033
Wouldn't it be great
if all this actually started

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:48.467
'cause some guy
didn't put his phone

00:02:48.467 --> 00:02:51.033
on airplane mode during takeoff?
[ Laughter ]

00:02:51.033 --> 00:02:55.534
"It's real?
This does something?"

00:02:55.534 --> 00:02:57.968
Of course, people were upset
about all the flight delays.

00:02:57.968 --> 00:02:59.100
Well, today, several airlines

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:00.667
made a statement
about the outage.

00:03:00.667 --> 00:03:02.167
For instance, Delta said...

00:03:04.901 --> 00:03:05.901
[ Laughter ]

00:03:05.901 --> 00:03:07.000
United said...

00:03:09.133 --> 00:03:11.067
[ Laughter ]
Southwest was like...

00:03:17.567 --> 00:03:19.000
[ Laughter ]
"Yeah."

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:20.501
And American Airlines said...

00:03:23.334 --> 00:03:24.868
And Southwest continued...

00:03:34.534 --> 00:03:36.834
Then JetBlue said...

00:03:38.601 --> 00:03:40.234
And finally Southwest said...

00:03:47.801 --> 00:03:48.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:48.868 --> 00:03:50.767
Windows 95?

00:03:50.767 --> 00:03:54.334
-Wow.

00:03:54.334 --> 00:03:56.200
-Well, hey, listen to this.
There was a report that the

00:03:56.200 --> 00:04:00.067
Biden administration was
considering a ban on gas stoves.

00:04:00.067 --> 00:04:01.267
I don't know
if you read about this.

00:04:01.267 --> 00:04:03.200
Well, after backlash
from both parties,

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:07.133
President Biden said that he is
not in favor of the idea.

00:04:07.133 --> 00:04:09.400
People stuck at airports
have said,

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:12.100
"I've been at JFK for nine
hours, but, by all means,

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:13.701
continue this
important discussion

00:04:13.701 --> 00:04:16.701
about gas freaking stoves!"
[ Laughter ]

00:04:16.701 --> 00:04:19.067
That's right, Biden said,
"You can keep your gas stove,

00:04:19.067 --> 00:04:21.567
but you have to wear an N95
while you use it."

00:04:21.567 --> 00:04:23.000
[ Laughter ]

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:25.434
Some more political news --
today, New York Republicans

00:04:25.434 --> 00:04:28.667
called on Congressman
George Santos to resign,

00:04:28.667 --> 00:04:31.767
and Santos responded,
saying he won't.

00:04:31.767 --> 00:04:34.901
But since it's Santos,
that means he will, maybe.

00:04:34.901 --> 00:04:36.934
[ Laughter ]

00:04:36.934 --> 00:04:39.200
Santos said he's not a quitter,
and he proved it

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:41.667
at the '92 Olympics,
where he won five gold medals.

00:04:41.667 --> 00:04:42.834
[ Laughter ]

00:04:42.834 --> 00:04:44.467
Well, get this,
after all the excitement

00:04:44.467 --> 00:04:46.033
over the speaker of the house
votes,

00:04:46.033 --> 00:04:48.567
C-SPAN wants to add
additional cameras

00:04:48.567 --> 00:04:50.334
in the chamber
so that it can cover

00:04:50.334 --> 00:04:51.868
more than just special events.

00:04:51.868 --> 00:04:53.701
They even released this message.
Take a look at this.

00:04:53.701 --> 00:04:57.234
-We here at C-SPAN are excited
to bring you even more coverage

00:04:57.234 --> 00:04:59.534
by adding additional cameras
to the chambers,

00:04:59.534 --> 00:05:01.367
including shots of the podiums,

00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:03.200
shots of the House
and Senate leaders,

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:06.167
and even a camera
in Bernie Sanders' eyebrows.

00:05:06.167 --> 00:05:08.934
-The price of Moderna
is too damn high!

00:05:08.934 --> 00:05:11.267
[ Applause ]

00:05:11.267 --> 00:05:14.634
-"The new Netflix"?
I don't know.

00:05:14.634 --> 00:05:17.167
Some entertainment news --
Coachella just announced

00:05:17.167 --> 00:05:19.734
all the artists performing
at this year's festival.

00:05:19.734 --> 00:05:21.100
And this is nice.
[ Cheers ]

00:05:21.100 --> 00:05:23.167
Yeah, they even went ahead
and paired each band

00:05:23.167 --> 00:05:24.834
with a perfect edible.
-Oh.

00:05:24.834 --> 00:05:26.467
[ Laughter ]

00:05:26.467 --> 00:05:28.834
-That's right, Coachella just
released this year's lineup,

00:05:28.834 --> 00:05:30.734
but it seems like
they took the name Coachella

00:05:30.734 --> 00:05:33.067
a bit more literal this year.
Watch this.

00:05:33.067 --> 00:05:36.234
-Coachella is back,
and we've got an incredible

00:05:36.234 --> 00:05:39.167
lineup this year,
including Bad Bunny,

00:05:39.167 --> 00:05:42.300
Frank Ocean, Blackpink,
Andy Reid, Pete Carroll,

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:45.901
Mike McCarthy, Phil Jackson,
Mike Krzyzewski, Bill Belichick,

00:05:45.901 --> 00:05:48.601
and America's favorite coach,
Craig T. Nelson.

00:05:48.601 --> 00:05:49.634
[ Air horns ]

00:05:49.634 --> 00:05:51.934
Coachella.
Don't miss it.

00:05:51.934 --> 00:05:53.767
-Just -- I find that --

00:05:53.767 --> 00:05:54.934
I'll see Craig T. Nelson.
-Yeah.

00:05:54.934 --> 00:05:56.067
-I'm down.

00:05:56.067 --> 00:05:58.434
Switching gears.
While the cost of other food

00:05:58.434 --> 00:06:01.267
has declined in recent months,
the price of eggs

00:06:01.267 --> 00:06:04.100
still remain extremely high.

00:06:04.100 --> 00:06:05.834
Now when you order eggs
in a diner, the waiter's like,

00:06:05.834 --> 00:06:07.667
"Get a load of Jeff Bezos
over here."

00:06:07.667 --> 00:06:08.667
[ Laughter ]

00:06:08.667 --> 00:06:11.033
"Mr. Three Eggs.
Must be nice, hey."

00:06:11.033 --> 00:06:15.100
[ Laughter ]

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:18.501
"Must be -- Must be nice with
those three eggs, this guy.

00:06:18.501 --> 00:06:21.501
Oh, wow."
[ Laughter ]

00:06:21.501 --> 00:06:23.000
It's hard finding cheap eggs.

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:24.834
This morning, I bought
a spinach and feta omelet

00:06:24.834 --> 00:06:26.267
out of the trunk
of some guy's car.

00:06:26.267 --> 00:06:27.534
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:06:27.534 --> 00:06:29.334
Meanwhile, I saw that Guinness
just announced

00:06:29.334 --> 00:06:31.534
that they're raising the price
of a pint in Ireland.

00:06:31.534 --> 00:06:32.767
-Ooh.

00:06:32.767 --> 00:06:35.767
-One politician suggested
drinking water instead.

00:06:35.767 --> 00:06:38.334
And doctors say he should be out
of the hospital by Sunday.

00:06:38.334 --> 00:06:39.767
[ Laughter ]

00:06:39.767 --> 00:06:42.868
Speaking of beverages,
Pepsi is replacing Sierra Mist

00:06:42.868 --> 00:06:44.934
with a new drink
to compete with Sprite,

00:06:44.934 --> 00:06:48.033
and it is called Starry.
Here's what it looks like.

00:06:48.033 --> 00:06:49.267
Yeah.

00:06:49.267 --> 00:06:51.534
It's called Starry,
and just like Sierra Mist,

00:06:51.534 --> 00:06:52.934
it's lemon-lime flavored

00:06:52.934 --> 00:06:55.300
and sounds like it was named
after a stripper.

00:06:55.300 --> 00:06:57.834
[ Laughter ]

00:06:57.834 --> 00:06:59.367
"Sierra Mist."

00:06:59.367 --> 00:07:00.467
[ Dance music plays ]

00:07:00.467 --> 00:07:03.300
[ Air horns ]

00:07:03.300 --> 00:07:04.133
[ Laughter ]

00:07:04.133 --> 00:07:05.868
-"Dr. Pepper."
-Yeah.

00:07:05.868 --> 00:07:08.767
[ Laughter ]

00:07:08.767 --> 00:07:10.934
They're all
named after soft drinks?

00:07:10.934 --> 00:07:13.767
Hey, did you guys hear about
the Mercedes recall?

00:07:13.767 --> 00:07:15.434
It's not good, dude.
Check this out.

00:07:15.434 --> 00:07:18.601
-An important recall alert
to tell you about this morning,

00:07:18.601 --> 00:07:23.634
as Mercedes-Benz sounds the
alarm over 124,000 vehicles

00:07:23.634 --> 00:07:28.167
whose sunroofs might suddenly
snap off while driving.

00:07:28.167 --> 00:07:30.801
-Oh, man!
I just bought a Mercedes-Benz.

00:07:30.801 --> 00:07:32.868
-Oh, really? Geez,
I'm sorry about that Tariq.

00:07:32.868 --> 00:07:35.634
-It's okay. I still have
my trusty Volkswagen Beetle,

00:07:35.634 --> 00:07:38.534
so I'm all good.

00:07:38.534 --> 00:07:41.200
-Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:41.200 --> 00:07:42.834
-"Oh," what?

00:07:42.834 --> 00:07:44.300
-Roll the clip.

00:07:44.300 --> 00:07:46.434
-Here's an important recall
alert for drivers this morning.

00:07:46.434 --> 00:07:49.734
Volkswagen recalling
nearly 40,000 of its Beetles

00:07:49.734 --> 00:07:51.868
because of faulty airbags.

00:07:51.868 --> 00:07:55.934
Inflators can explode with too
much force and hurl shrapnel.

00:07:55.934 --> 00:07:57.100
-What?!
[ Laughter ]

00:07:57.100 --> 00:07:59.534
-Yeah, that -- that's not good.

00:07:59.534 --> 00:08:01.601
-How am I supposed
to get around this week?

00:08:01.601 --> 00:08:03.133
-You don't have any other way?

00:08:03.133 --> 00:08:05.934
-I mean,
I have an old four-wheeler.

00:08:05.934 --> 00:08:09.234
I guess I could dust off
my Polaris Sportsman

00:08:09.234 --> 00:08:11.901
and Scrambler 1000 S
all-terrain vehicle.

00:08:11.901 --> 00:08:13.834
-Polaris is recalling
the Sportsman

00:08:13.834 --> 00:08:17.200
and Scrambler 1000 S
all-terrain vehicles.

00:08:17.200 --> 00:08:19.501
-Come on!
-I'm -- I'm sorry, Tariq.

00:08:19.501 --> 00:08:21.000
There's gotta be something
you can do.

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:23.567
-No.
N-No, Jimmy.

00:08:23.567 --> 00:08:26.701
I'm just gonna stay at home
and sit back and enjoy

00:08:26.701 --> 00:08:33.801
some Member's Mark holiday
m-macarons sold at Sam's Club.

00:08:33.801 --> 00:08:34.934
-A consumer alert for you --

00:08:34.934 --> 00:08:38.300
Member's Mark
holiday m-macarons

00:08:38.300 --> 00:08:39.934
sold at Sam's Club
are being recalled.

00:08:39.934 --> 00:08:44.334
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:44.334 --> 00:08:47.167
-This January is a bust!

00:08:47.167 --> 00:08:48.934
-There's gotta be something
you can do.

00:08:48.934 --> 00:08:50.634
-Well, is anything safe?

00:08:50.634 --> 00:08:52.934
I'm gonna have to go
buy groceries in Kansas

00:08:52.934 --> 00:08:56.701
and only eat Sunsprouts --
[ Swallows ] -- from now on.

00:08:56.701 --> 00:08:59.000
-We have a recall alert.
If you buy groceries in Kansas,

00:08:59.000 --> 00:09:02.033
Sunsprouts -- [ Swallows ] --
is recalling 1,400 pounds

00:09:02.033 --> 00:09:05.901
of alfalfa sprouts.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:05.901 --> 00:09:07.534
-That's it.

00:09:07.534 --> 00:09:09.133
That's it, man.
I'm locking myself inside,

00:09:09.133 --> 00:09:11.734
just me and my washing machine,

00:09:11.734 --> 00:09:14.834
safe from all problems
and potential "janjer."

00:09:14.834 --> 00:09:16.601
-A washing machine recall.

00:09:16.601 --> 00:09:19.000
The problem
and the potential "janjer."

00:09:19.000 --> 00:09:22.934
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:22.934 --> 00:09:29.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:29.601 --> 00:09:32.667
-So close.
[ Both laugh ]

00:09:32.667 --> 00:09:34.434
So close.
-Yeah.

00:09:34.434 --> 00:09:36.267
-Stay out of --

00:09:36.267 --> 00:09:38.434
Tariq Trotter doesn't want to
get any "janjer" over there.

00:09:38.434 --> 00:09:40.367
Tariq Trotter.
Thank you.

00:09:40.367 --> 00:09:46.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:46.267 --> 00:09:48.934
Hey, guys, I read that surgeons
are warning against

00:09:48.934 --> 00:09:50.801
leg-lengthening surgery...

00:09:50.801 --> 00:09:52.000
[ Laughter ]

00:09:52.000 --> 00:09:54.734
...a procedure that has become
popular with men.

00:09:54.734 --> 00:09:56.200
Yeah, it's very expensive.

00:09:56.200 --> 00:09:58.167
In order to get approved
by your insurance company,

00:09:58.167 --> 00:10:00.567
you have to prove that nobody
is swiping right on your Tinder.

00:10:00.567 --> 00:10:03.167
[ Laughter ]

00:10:03.167 --> 00:10:04.834
And finally,
according to experts,

00:10:04.834 --> 00:10:08.734
the friendliest city in the U.S.
is Honolulu.

00:10:08.734 --> 00:10:11.367
Unfortunately, since "aloha"
also means goodbye,

00:10:11.367 --> 00:10:13.467
Honolulu is also
the least friendliest city.

00:10:13.467 --> 00:10:15.467
[ Laughter and applause ]
We have a great show tonight!

